{
    "word": "monoecious",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "cc2fbbe4-40f3-31c4-9ae6-69484852e6d2",
                "word": "monoecious",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "32b0c375-01d2-350a-85b2-5a118203b228",
                        "entry_id": "cc2fbbe4-40f3-31c4-9ae6-69484852e6d2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Having both the male and female reproductive organs in the same individual, either in different flowers or in the same or different flowers; hermaphrodite."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7ecb3cef-f939-4c72-a770-37965cd5df21",
                                "sense_id": "32b0c375-01d2-350a-85b2-5a118203b228",
                                "text": "Further, species which show continuous variation that is not amenable to orthodox taxonomic treatment, and this is the situation in many monoecious plants, are treated as invariable."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f348fa27-3019-4396-8eab-533ba4d752c2",
                                "sense_id": "32b0c375-01d2-350a-85b2-5a118203b228",
                                "text": "Recently, monoecious plants have been found in several places in the United States. The plants of Australia are monoecious and dioecious."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "21bdd582-fa36-47b1-a402-3a21fdff4f4a",
                                "sense_id": "32b0c375-01d2-350a-85b2-5a118203b228",
                                "text": "Two factors are likely to allow the establishment of forms with reduced pollen output (i.e., fewer male flowers) in a monoecious population: increased seed fitness as a result of an increase in the ratio of female to male flowers, and a reduced rate of self-fertilisation."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "83563860-c0aa-4ca6-8c12-11651c77db43",
                        "source_entry_id": "cc2fbbe4-40f3-31c4-9ae6-69484852e6d2",
                        "source_sense_id": "32b0c375-01d2-350a-85b2-5a118203b228",
                        "source_sense_description": "having the male and female reproductive organs on different parts of the same plant",
                        "target_lang_word": "monoïque",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "monoïque",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "df688fc3-7ee5-330a-a587-8d2d57d68dfd",
                                        "entry_id": "b8c8b288-e30e-34b5-a569-83be4c088f53",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Se dit d’une espèce dont les fleurs unisexuées mâles (à étamines) et femelles (à pistil) sont portées par le même pied. Cela permet la fécondation croisée (allogamie)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0fcb02a2-869a-4489-b077-e921bbfcaab7",
                                                "sense_id": "df688fc3-7ee5-330a-a587-8d2d57d68dfd",
                                                "text": "Les mots de bissexuel et d’unisexuel, d’hermaphrodite et d’androgyne, de monoïque et de dioïque, de polygame et de dichogame… etc., n'atteignent guère jusqu'à la subtilité des distinctions qui demanderaient à être faites."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2cf44923-bcae-4652-9991-89c81bca7f2d",
                                                "sense_id": "df688fc3-7ee5-330a-a587-8d2d57d68dfd",
                                                "text": "La Laîche à épis pendants est une plante monoïque qui fleurit de mai à juillet."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1a207b24-4e2b-4c7c-858b-3a92f7cc9143",
                        "source_entry_id": "cc2fbbe4-40f3-31c4-9ae6-69484852e6d2",
                        "source_sense_id": "32b0c375-01d2-350a-85b2-5a118203b228",
                        "source_sense_description": "having the male and female reproductive organs on different parts of the same plant",
                        "target_lang_word": "monözisch",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "monözisch",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cf14f7fb-29c7-3907-90ad-270a305d3c2f",
                                        "entry_id": "f826049b-fd5c-36d7-89c1-863cdc8630ee",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "männliche und weibliche Blüten auf einem Individuum vorkommend"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Pflanzen"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "58ccf6e8-4eaa-4ab8-acc0-f53fa28cdd00",
                                                "sense_id": "cf14f7fb-29c7-3907-90ad-270a305d3c2f",
                                                "text": "Ein Organismus ist monözisch, wenn beide sexuell differenzierten Gametentypen auf einem Indiviuum produziert werden; diözisch, wenn jedes Individuum nur Gameten eines Typs produziert."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4b7443ff-9fac-424e-9488-f649d0c6a2c7",
                                                "sense_id": "cf14f7fb-29c7-3907-90ad-270a305d3c2f",
                                                "text": "Wie diözische Pflanzen besitzen auch die monözischen nur eingeschlechtige Blüten."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d961b06f-34ab-4686-a40d-fc60a459b0f0",
                                                "sense_id": "cf14f7fb-29c7-3907-90ad-270a305d3c2f",
                                                "text": "Die Moose können sowohl monözisch als auch diözisch oder zwittrig sein."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5575efd3-d7e3-48c4-ab2e-68831bad27a3",
                                                "sense_id": "cf14f7fb-29c7-3907-90ad-270a305d3c2f",
                                                "text": "Bei Kulturpflanzen wurden in einigen Fällen jedoch monözische Sorten aus den ursprünglich diözischen Arten gezüchtet, so bei der Weinrebe Vitis vinifera und beim Hanf (Cannabis sativa)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d174607e-c03c-45fe-8464-056215a98282",
                                                "sense_id": "cf14f7fb-29c7-3907-90ad-270a305d3c2f",
                                                "text": "Bei monözischen (einhäusigen) Pilzen kann das aus einer Spore gewachsene Mycel als Kernakzeptor und -donator dienen, da es Kerne beiderlei Geschlechts enthält."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
